der more carefully. \n\nI realize now the table provides both on-budget and off-budget outlays for each agency, but they're presented in a combined format. The key is to find separate values for each budget type. I'll need to dig deeper into the data sources to extract the precise on-budget and off-budget figures for the Department of Commerce across those fiscal years.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_9bcd8111dd4b49288ccece65","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"Commerce.*On-Budget\\|Commerce.*Off-Budget\" /app/resources/treasury_bulletin_2024_12.txt"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
